pragma Singleton

import QtQuick

// The icon set.
//
// Material Symbols, Rounded style. The icons are a font: a font is
// the best renderer there is for a glyph, because it is hinted for
// the size it is drawn at, it takes its colour from the text, and
// it comes with the variable axes the icons were designed around
// -- FILL for the filled variants, wght for the weight.
//
// The names below are the shell's own, kebab-case and stable;
// `ligatures` is the translation into the names the font knows.
//
// The path data is the fallback, for a machine without the font
// installed. It is the same artwork, taken from the font's own
// outlines, but Qt's shape renderer flattens the curves at the
// path's own resolution rather than at the size being drawn, so it
// is rougher than the font is.
